{
  "name": "zzz-test — QRSalt node, every operation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## QRSalt — full node test\n\n**Before you press Execute**\n1. Make a credential of type *QRSalt API* and call it exactly **QRSalt account**, so every node below binds to it on import. If you called it something else, pick it on the first QRSalt node and n8n will offer to use it everywhere.\n2. The key needs the **delete** scope and a plan with API access; the delete steps fail otherwise and the summary says so.\n3. To test the scan trigger as well, import **zzz-trigger-test.json** and switch it on first — this run fires a real scan on the link it makes.\n\n**What it does**: every operation of the node, in an order that works — create, use, then delete. Everything it makes is named `zzz-test-<timestamp>-…`.\n\n**Afterwards**: open the **Summary** node and copy the single `report` field. The run cleans up after itself: every object it made is deleted again.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-readme",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -820,
        -320
      ]
